# SMC Scratchpad RAM sanity preload — SystemC test fixture.
#
# One 64-bit word per line in big-endian ASCII hex (MSB first).
# Blank lines and `#`-prefixed comments are ignored, matching the upstream
# hex format produced by the SMC tooling.
#
# A preload is optional for a scratchpad (it normally cold-boots to zero);
# this fixture lets the test bench verify the preload pipeline and read-back.
#
# Word 0
0011223344556677
# Word 1
8899aabbccddeeff
# Word 2
0123456789abcdef
# Word 3
fedcba9876543210
# Words 4..6: zero padding (also implicit; exercises the parser's
# blank-data-word path).
0000000000000000
0000000000000000
0000000000000000
# Word 7: sentinel — verifies sparse non-zero placement at offset > 0.
0000deadbeef1234
